    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d597">

                <pb facs="d596-2" n="2" sameAs="frus:frus1958-60v03mSupp/d596-2"/>

                <head>597. Letter From Herter to Gray<anchor n="1" xml:id="d597-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1960-09-14">September 14,
                        1960</date></dateline>
                    <salute>Dear Gordon:</salute>
                </opener>
                <pb facs="d597-1" n="1" type="facsimile" xml:id="d597-1"/>
                <p>I was most happy to receive your comments of September 13 on the suggested letter
                    from the President and the statement of functions <pb facs="2274" n="2169"
                        type="typeset" xml:id="pg2169"/> of the new U.S. Disarmament Administration.
                    I am in general agreement with your suggestions and have asked that appropriate
                    changes be made in the two documents in the light of such comments as we receive
                    from the agencies concerned.</p>
                <p>With warmest personal regards,</p>
                <p>Most sincerely,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold">Christian A. Herter</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>






